  "notes": "Cause code officially TBD/provisional per form fields; root cause of 'dirty contacts' stated as unknown in narrative. Past operability review extended the inoperability window back to first identification in CR 2023-30437 (05/23/2023), spanning ~10 months, though the triggering CR that changed the operability conclusion was CR 2024-36970 on 03/17/2024 (the event date). No block_13 data provided in form fields (empty array), so component/system/manufacturer codes not tabulated there but captured from narrative text. HPCI itself remained operable throughout; only the PCIV function of E4150-F042 was inoperable. No previous occurrences per report despite prior CRs 2023-30437 and 2024-36518 addressing same condition with inaccurate operability conclusions -- these are not modeled as SIMILAR_TO stub LERs since they are internal condition reports, not LERs, and the narrative explicitly states 'PREVIOUS OCCURRENCES: None'."
